# Graphify scope follows the Git exclusion policy, plus two widenings of its
# own further down: lockfiles and media/binary assets are dropped to keep the
# index cheap (see those sections). The agent layer is NOT one of them —
# .agents/, AGENTS.md, .omp/ and docs/ are unshipped, so indexing them only
# pushed their symbols into the tracked graph.json: 349 of 4278 nodes came
# from .agents/. The tracked graph is a map of the code that ships.

# Generic agent instructions, harness state, and local plans
.agent/
.omp/
.codex/
.claude/
AGENTS.md
conductor/

# Include test source and project docs; omit captured fixture payloads.
/tests/fixtures/
/docs/heap-snapshots/
/docs/har/
/docs/

# Graphify Outputs (prevent self-indexing)
graphify-out/

# Git Worktrees (prevent duplicate tree indexing)
.worktrees/

# Dependencies & Lockfiles
node_modules/
package-lock.json
uv.lock
mise.lock
.venv/
.uv/
